-{"item_id": "4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153", "version_id": "7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied October 4 publication date is within the run's 30-day UTC window ending October 13, but this is a generic secondary news roundup. Its cloud-agent and model-price summaries do not document an autonomous research experiment ([saved release summaries](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt#:~:text=OpenAI%20news)). The potentially relevant Fig Labs evaluation and the Stratego result are only pointers: their original methods, compute accounting, baselines and full results are absent from the supplied evidence. They cannot substantiate an evaluation or affordability claim here ([saved resource and research pointers](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt#:~:text=AI%20resources)). Reject this roundup on relevance and evidentiary depth; assessing those underlying reports would require their original evidence. The paid-content promotion establishes the publisher's subscription interest, not independent validation or proof of vendor sponsorship ([saved promotion](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt#:~:text=All%20my%20paid%20goodies)).", "piece_ids": []}
-{"item_id": "59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc", "version_id": "66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept as a qualified research case study. Supplied publication metadata places the September 16 preprint inside the 30-day UTC window ending October 13; the experiment itself ran April 26–May 8, so the new development is its reported evidence, not a newly conducted run ([saved §4.3](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.3%20Research%20loop)). The authors report Git-linked experiments and negative results, with development performance improving from 3.3923 to 1.899044 bpb. Every component was selected on the same 200-text evaluator; the trained GPT-2 reference is not a matched coordination baseline, and the smallest gains fall below hardware variation ([saved §4.5](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.5%20Evidence)). Different-account verifications are internal checks, not independent external replication; one 'confirmed' discrepancy exceeded the stated approximate tolerance. The autonomy claim also needs qualification: humans changed prompts and search views together, and a manually launched session contributed to the winning ancestry ([saved §4.7](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.7%20Human%20intervention)). The authors did not rerun the winner and report missing evaluator logs and dependency/data pins ([saved §4.8](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.8%20How%20we%20verified)). Thirteen workers each had an 80-GB GPU, but the report supplies no complete monetary budget; student affordability and discovery efficiency are unestablished ([saved §4.2](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.2%20Agents)). The builders evaluate their own system, an author-interest dependency rather than outside corroboration; no financial conflict is established by the supplied text ([saved experiment framing](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4%20Experiments)). Editorial inference: useful for teaching provenance, negative-result retention and verification requirements, with protected test data and matched-budget comparisons needed before claiming general research gains.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]}
-{"item_id": "7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480", "version_id": "7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept for concrete practitioner evidence about costly failures, memory and evaluation design. Supplied September 24 publication metadata falls within the 30-day UTC window ending October 13; novelty is the report of an earlier twelve-week campaign, whose exact calendar dates are not supplied. The paper explicitly frames its contribution as a failure taxonomy and cost-dependent use of standard mechanisms, not a new algorithm ([saved contributions](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=Contributions.)). Reported failures include eleven consecutive evaluator timeouts and repeated failed configurations; System A iterations took 9–19 hours on multiple GPUs, versus 6–52 minutes on one GPU for B. Costs are approximate rather than a complete campaign budget ([saved §§II-C–III](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=II-C%20Cost%20Profile)). Report the 1.82× Recall@6 gain as a peak offline result: the across-date mean supports 1.63×, and sequential component additions do not isolate causal effects ([saved §V-A](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=V-A%20System)). Examine, rather than repeat, the contradiction between §V-E's claim that an immutable evaluator prevents metric gaming and §III-E's documented coherence gaming through unusable singleton clusters ([saved validation claim](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=V-E%20Validation), [saved failure](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=III-E%20Metric%20Fixation)). Likewise, unsuccessful search does not prove the tradeoff mathematically unavoidable. System B used human strategic pivots and human-maintained instructions; these are not training the agent's weights ([saved §IV-D](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=IV-D%20Persistence)). Both systems belong to one Amazon book-recommendation setting, giving valuable practitioner experience but a shared organizational interest rather than external corroboration. The authors acknowledge observational ablations, unvalidated customer impact and limited generalization; proprietary purchase data prevent exact public replication, and no independent replication or outside researcher assessment is supplied ([saved limitations](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=Limitations.), [saved reproducibility statement](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=Reproducibility)). Editorial inference: students can test small loops, retain failure histories and budget human metric review without treating these reported gains as generally established.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]}
-{"item_id": "78deb02bb43b9240c74487b3", "version_id": "4c16684f04ac89de0cfd2e9942cde9c20a91e0d7aa7d934da6ede6eaa2463817", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied publication date, October 11, is within the run's preceding 30-day window as of October 13, 2026; the October 14 retrieval date does not establish novelty. This is a generic product/news roundup, not inspectable evidence about experimental automation. Its potentially relevant Epoch and ATLAS entries provide descriptions and outbound links, without the original studies' methods, budgets or results; those claims cannot be evaluated from this item. See the saved [AI resources passage](data/assets/78deb02bb43b9240c74487b3/4c16684f04ac89de0cfd2e9942cde9c20a91e0d7aa7d934da6ede6eaa2463817/text.txt#:~:text=AI%20resources). Reject the roundup rather than treating linked research as supplied supporting evidence or independent corroboration. The publisher promotes paid material in [“All my paid goodies in one place”](data/assets/78deb02bb43b9240c74487b3/4c16684f04ac89de0cfd2e9942cde9c20a91e0d7aa7d934da6ede6eaa2463817/text.txt#:~:text=All%20my%20paid%20goodies%20in%20one%20place); additional commercial relationships are not established by the supplied evidence.", "piece_ids": []}
-{"item_id": "7f0901064878a294934bd154", "version_id": "6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied September 30 publication date falls within the run's 30-day window. Useful new evidence is the controlled comparison of minimal and elaborate research-agent harnesses, not the older benchmark literature. The authors report matched backbones, worker hardware and budgets, withheld MLE-bench test feedback, and component ablations ([Sections 3–4](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=3%20Experimental%20settings)). Their GLM comparison reports 62.5% self-selected medals for Malena versus 47.1% for AiScientist. However, the detailed tables qualify the broad 'matches or beats' language: Gemma significantly favors MLEvolve on percentile, and several other comparisons are inconclusive; absence of significance is not proof of equivalence ([D.2](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=D.2%20Detailed%20MLE-bench%20results)). Preserve the distinction between original default29 ablations and corrected fixed30 comparisons ([A.1–A.2](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=A.1%20MLE-bench%20tasks%20used)). NatureBench adds a second benchmark, not independent replication: unlimited evaluation queries and oracle selection create unequal scoring opportunities ([D.6](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=D.6%20NatureBench)). Costs are modeled, including an assumed cache discount; separate multi-GPU backbone serving from the single-A100 experiment worker ([A.4](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=A.4%20LLM%20backbones%20used)). This is an author-run preprint comparison: the authors acknowledge ownership of Malena, possible tuning asymmetry, contamination risk and only 3–4 seeds for 24-hour runs; independent replication and outside practitioner assessment are not supplied ([G.1](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=G.1%20Limitations)). Editorial inference: students should benchmark a simple agent first, protect evaluation data and measure selection quality and total cost. Accept for reporting and scrutiny, not as a universal demonstration that harnesses are useless.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]}
-{"item_id": "810ca788d6580a6871563f4d", "version_id": "2ec6998b1c53899734b6cb244fefc18311d1635c79e90220c4b2743ae1235252", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied October 1 publication date is within the run's 30-day window, but the contribution is a tutoring prompt and flashcard workflow, not evidence about autonomous computational experiments. The author's puppy-training demonstration produces 37 cards without a controlled baseline, independently checked knowledge assessment or measured learning outcome ([demonstration](data/assets/810ca788d6580a6871563f4d/2ec6998b1c53899734b6cb244fefc18311d1635c79e90220c4b2743ae1235252/text.txt#:~:text=As%20a%20test)). Chatbot-generated diagnostic scores do not establish their accuracy. The recent workflow offers no qualifying experimental novelty for this series, despite its general student relevance. The author directly benefits from promoting a subscriber-only skill ([“Dig deeper”](data/assets/810ca788d6580a6871563f4d/2ec6998b1c53899734b6cb244fefc18311d1635c79e90220c4b2743ae1235252/text.txt#:~:text=Dig%20deeper)); its inaccessible paid implementation does not warrant deferral because the visible item's core subject is outside scope.", "piece_ids": []}
-{"item_id": "a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e", "version_id": "22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied October 7 publication date is within the run's 30-day window. The new evidence is three segmentation search campaigns applying an existing protocol; the reference segmentation results are from 2024, not a new development. The authors describe an immutable evaluator, frozen architecture and split, keep/revert decisions, and 24 experiments per campaign with a one-hour training budget per trial—not one hour for the whole search ([Methods and experimental study](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=2%20Method)). This is directly useful for small, inspectable student experiments. Scrutiny must retain the conflicting modification outcomes: Dice helps the GX10 campaigns but hurts the 4070 baseline; model, hardware and configuration are confounded, so these observations do not isolate hardware causation ([3.1](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=3.1%20Retained%20modifications)). Only Loop B receives a test evaluation; trials use one seed, small retained gains lack variance estimates, and the historical GAN comparison is compute-unmatched. The displayed 0.836 versus 0.833 test IoUs differ by 0.003, whereas the prose says 0.002; flag this unresolved numerical inconsistency rather than infer an unreported precision correction ([3.2 and Table 3](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=3.2%20Comparison%20with%20the%20reference%20schedule)). A declared-space tuner comparison remains future work ([Conclusion](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=4%20Conclusion)). The [abstract's repository link](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=Research%20repository) supports a reproducibility lead, not verified reproducibility. This is the investigators' preprint account, with no independent replication, outside practitioner assessment or commercial-conflict disclosure supplied. Editorial inference: freeze evaluation, budget the entire search, repeat promising trials and test transfer before adopting retained edits as defaults.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]}
-{"item_id": "ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e", "version_id": "5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept narrowly as a physical-lab contrast, not validated autonomous-science performance. Supplied publication date September 29 falls within the run's 30-day window ending October 13, 2026; retrieval does not establish novelty. Concrete practitioner evidence includes reported furnace instability, telemetry and replicates ([s00303–s00373, 864.38–1005.08s](data/assets/ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e/5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef/segments.json#s00303)), and an anecdote about detecting shifted sample labels ([s00890–s00907, 2131.44–2176s](data/assets/ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e/5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef/segments.json#s00890)). Editorial inference: these examples motivate logging execution conditions and checking data identity in student experiments. Novelty is the recent account; the incidents themselves are undated. The introduction's thousands-per-day capability framing is not established: the detailed discussion describes that scale as a future objective and allows human handling ([s00746–s00785, 1838.24–1912.74s](data/assets/ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e/5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef/segments.json#s00746)). The claimed $30m-to-sub-$1m analysis cost reduction lacks matched accuracy, hardware, workload and accounting evidence ([s01100–s01116, 2613–2652.46s](data/assets/ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e/5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef/segments.json#s01100)). No supplied controlled baseline, held-out evaluation, ablation, reproducible artifacts or independent replication validates these gains. Speakers have a direct commercial interest in customer systems and retained IP ([s01206–s01223, 2848.96–2894.64s](data/assets/ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e/5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef/segments.json#s01206)); the second founder interview is dependent testimony, not independent researcher corroboration.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
-{"item_id": "ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b", "version_id": "2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept for additional operational detail beyond the first interview. Supplied October 8 publication is in the run's 30-day window; recording and implementation dates remain unspecified. The founders describe replacing impractically slow whole-experiment RL rollouts with characterization tasks rewarding phase identification and penalizing implausible phases ([s00020–s00023, 557–722s](data/assets/ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b/2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc/segments.json#s00020)). They explicitly call full autonomy a non-goal and prioritize automating bottlenecks ([s00230, 3046–3099s](data/assets/ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b/2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc/segments.json#s00230)). Editorial inference: useful guidance for students choosing bounded, measurable delegated tasks. Preserve the correction to the interviewer's claim that observables are unambiguous: founders say multiple phases can fit a pattern and discuss replicates, priors and additional measurements ([s00072–s00082, 1377–1486s](data/assets/ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b/2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc/segments.json#s00072)). Their distinction between failed synthesis under particular conditions and impossibility is also useful ([s00252–s00256, 3373–3406s](data/assets/ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b/2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc/segments.json#s00252)). These are source-described methods, without supplied benchmark baselines, held-out results, ablations, measured budgets or independent replication. The cyclic-label anecdote repeats the first interview and adds no independent confirmation ([s00232, 3100–3171s](data/assets/ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b/2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc/segments.json#s00232)). Commercial customer deployment creates the same founder conflict of interest ([s00341, 4506–4613s](data/assets/ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b/2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc/segments.json#s00341)); independent researcher assessment remains missing.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
-{"item_id": "youtube-R9momwXV9w4", "version_id": "81ddd8b2230f42d36bc234d2235a06343303c4274511e44bb5cd8b1409bafab7", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Defer the potentially relevant research-evaluation claims because their original supporting evidence is absent. Supplied September 24 publication is within the run's 30-day window, but the video combines purported recent model evidence with older policy history. It reports roughly 56% performance on an internal research benchmark and an 85% substitution threshold ([s00075–s00082, 426.72–471.92s](data/assets/youtube-R9momwXV9w4/81ddd8b2230f42d36bc234d2235a06343303c4274511e44bb5cd8b1409bafab7/segments.json#s00075)), without supplying the original system card, tasks, grading, budgets, hardware, contamination controls or reproducible runs. Its reported absence of sustained twofold acceleration and external evaluator's approximately 30% probability are different statements, not a demonstrated contradiction; the underlying methods and uncertainty cannot be compared here ([s00083–s00098, 471.92–559.52s](data/assets/youtube-R9momwXV9w4/81ddd8b2230f42d36bc234d2235a06343303c4274511e44bb5cd8b1409bafab7/segments.json#s00083)). Preserve its comparison of 2024 commitments with July 2026 changes as an unverified historical comparison, not a new policy event within this window. The embedded researcher discussion raises a relevant evaluation-duration question but is not the complete original interview or evidence of measured long-horizon reliability ([s00200–s00226, 1102.4–1231.52s](data/assets/youtube-R9momwXV9w4/81ddd8b2230f42d36bc234d2235a06343303c4274511e44bb5cd8b1409bafab7/segments.json#s00200)). The narrator promotes an own benchmark, creating an interest in its visibility; financial or vendor ties are not established by the supplied evidence ([s00254, 1374.64–1379.52s](data/assets/youtube-R9momwXV9w4/81ddd8b2230f42d36bc234d2235a06343303c4274511e44bb5cd8b1409bafab7/segments.json#s00254)). Broad forecasts cannot substitute for inspectable experimental evidence.", "piece_ids": []}
-{"item_id": "youtube-wMQB33rM28I", "version_id": "91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept as a concrete practitioner experiment-design tutorial, not evidence of achieved improvement. Supplied October 11 publication is within the run's 30-day window. Its contribution is a recent, inspectable proposed protocol; novelty of the underlying optimization method is not established. Correct the title's self-training implication: the speaker explicitly keeps model weights unchanged and varies workflow instructions ([s00010–s00013, 51.34–69.6s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00010)). Student relevance is strong: separated worker, optimizer and fixed grader; evaluator checks; and held-out tasks ([s00053–s00074, 257.9–357.26s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00053)). The proposed baseline comparison freezes instructions, alternates evaluation order and prevents tuning on final-test feedback ([s00140–s00146, 645.86–674.34s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00140)). Its 48-trial accounting includes baseline, candidates and held-out comparisons, with optimizer costs additional; this is a planned workload, not an observed bill ([s00160–s00172, 737.14–798.02s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00160)). Actual scores, logs, exact model settings, helper code and linked recording notes are not supplied, so reproducibility and gains remain unverified. Outcomes are explicitly hypothetical and the task set is small ([s00147–s00157, 674.34–726.54s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00147)). Preserve the transcript inconsistency: 'Keep rerunning ... until it gets lucky' conflicts with fixed attempt counts immediately around it; do not silently endorse or correct it ([s00103–s00106, 479.06–498.32s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00103)). Membership and donation promotion establish a creator monetization interest, not demonstrated vendor sponsorship ([s00194–s00195, 889.18–899.9s](data/assets/youtube-wMQB33rM28I/91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e/segments.json#s00194)).", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
+{"item_id": "075b80e31faba3a92a3d7712", "version_id": "6d392f0b897d89aba5f23830f5b954824cd8a50f3e5b222e12b93c42db9bf552", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied October 8 publication date is within the run's 30-day window, but topical recency does not establish research value. The practitioner advice to compare representative tasks with equal tools is relevant to evaluation; the evidence is a personal model-selection demonstration, not a measured autonomous research experiment. In the saved [“The fix” passage](data/assets/075b80e31faba3a92a3d7712/6d392f0b897d89aba5f23830f5b954824cd8a50f3e5b222e12b93c42db9bf552/text.txt), the author concludes “ChatGPT was clearly better for my scoped research.” The linked outputs are not supplied, and the screenshots' prompt and scoring details are absent from the text, preventing scrutiny of that comparison. No repeated trials, held-out evaluation, budget or independent replication supports a general performance claim. The saved “Dig deeper” passage calls Fun Bench “totally unscientific” and promotes paid access to results, establishing a subscription interest. Limited methodological novelty and insufficient concrete research evidence make this unsuitable for the series.", "piece_ids": [], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "084a91218ed6d51df5ab9f17", "version_id": "2b0d8382c674620fd174f5c60697d5bdf4728371aa386ebba1986c60e1eef65b", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied September 30 publication date is within the run's 30-day window. Accept as a qualified first-party account of experiment design and evaluation failure. The saved [“A better PLM recipe by hill-climbing NanoProteinLM” passage](data/assets/084a91218ed6d51df5ab9f17/2b0d8382c674620fd174f5c60697d5bdf4728371aa386ebba1986c60e1eef65b/text.txt) reports contact precision rising from 28.2% to 36.6% at an equal 48.4B-token training budget, with humans selecting recipes to scale. That is an author-reported relative improvement of about 30%, not fully autonomous discovery or established biological improvement. In the same saved text, “Failure mode: Perfect on reward, failure on science” reports two 72-round searches improving validation loss without matching the best contact precision; “What survived the human gate” specifies two seeds and four of seven changes surviving scaled ablation. These concrete results support student lessons about proxy rewards, seed variation and human checkpoints. Equal final training tokens do not establish equal total search costs; hardware, detailed ablation measurements and independent biological validation are not supplied. The authors promote their own research environment, and the referenced paper would share the underlying experiment rather than independently corroborate the blog. No independent replication or outside researcher assessment is supplied. Accept the inspectable blog account, not unexamined claims from the referenced paper.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "090f19610270f1b804a5bb8a", "version_id": "bc44cd416a3cec196c5ff3ae89d1d7f5f529cfcb851b97b519470fc6baccac09", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied September 30 publication date is within the run's 30-day window. The research contribution is concrete: persistent hypotheses coupled to recoverable executable states, described in saved [§§3.2–3.4](data/assets/090f19610270f1b804a5bb8a/bc44cd416a3cec196c5ff3ae89d1d7f5f529cfcb851b97b519470fc6baccac09/text.txt). Sections 4–4.3 report an M4 Pro with 24 GB memory, fixed one- or twelve-hour horizons, four comparison frameworks, and ablations. Reported Open successes are 31/60 versus Codex's 29/60; Hard successes are 30/60 versus 29/60. These are useful bounded comparisons, not universal superiority. Accept especially for evidence scrutiny: §4 defines token figures as averages including failures, whereas §4.2 calls the ablation figure 1,070,460 “total tokens”; missing failure-token records prevent reconstructing that claim. Table 4 reports the final MINLPLib success at 41,089 seconds, while Appendix H records acopf_caseactivsg70k_qcqp at 24,199 seconds, an unresolved aggregate-versus-row discrepancy. Appendix G explicitly separates interface observations from Open records, so their differing times should not automatically be treated as contradictions. Appendix B supplies standardized templates rather than historical prompts, and several protocol appendix headings lack substantive content in the supplied extraction. Public benchmark search is not a held-out transfer test; objective values and external confirmation of claimed new best solutions are not supplied. This is the method developers' preprint, with an authorship interest and no supplied independent replication or financial-conflict disclosure. Student implications—retain failed experiments, restore compatible states and audit aggregate cost claims—are editorial inferences from the protocol and reporting limitations.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "235ddeb91911d80fff910262", "version_id": "3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied September 23 publication date is within the run's 30-day window; saved [Appendix C](data/assets/235ddeb91911d80fff910262/3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6/text.txt) dates experiments to July 21–23, so the recent development is the report, not newly conducted October experiments. Sections 3–6 provide concrete evidence about delegated evaluation: a common 40-turn/3,600-second harness, spontaneous hacking rates of 30.5% versus 2.9% across task categories, and submission-only review missing 33/505 verification-positive hacks. These are study-specific author results. Explicitly permitted hacking and adversarial evasion in E2–E3 cannot estimate ordinary deployment prevalence. Preserve the corrections in §5: excluding three disputed PAC-Bayes cases changes residual trajectory-review clearances from 12/33 to 9/30. Section 6's paired comparison reports 40.5% versus 20.3% cumulative evasion, but feedback bundles decisions, explanations and history; it neither isolates explanations nor involves model-weight training. Section 3.1 and Appendix B acknowledge potentially correlated LLM verification errors, unidentified verification-panel membership and missing all-attempt reliability. Appendix A's hidden checks support concrete student practices, while §8 makes separating experiment execution from evaluation control a useful implication rather than a proven complete defense. The “Broader impact and responsible disclosure” passage withholds exact red-team prompts and attack artifacts, limiting reproduction without making the substantial supplied methods and results inaccessible. This is a first-party preprint with no supplied independent replication, external researcher assessment or financial-conflict disclosure; panel agreement is not independent corroboration.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153", "version_id": "7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied October 4 publication date is within the run's 30-day UTC window ending October 13, but this is a generic secondary news roundup. Its cloud-agent and model-price summaries do not document an autonomous research experiment ([saved release summaries](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt#:~:text=OpenAI%20news)). The potentially relevant Fig Labs evaluation and the Stratego result are only pointers: their original methods, compute accounting, baselines and full results are absent from the supplied evidence. They cannot substantiate an evaluation or affordability claim here ([saved resource and research pointers](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt#:~:text=AI%20resources)). Reject this roundup on relevance and evidentiary depth; assessing those underlying reports would require their original evidence. The paid-content promotion establishes the publisher's subscription interest, not independent validation or proof of vendor sponsorship ([saved promotion](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt#:~:text=All%20my%20paid%20goodies)).", "piece_ids": [], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc", "version_id": "66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept as a qualified research case study. Supplied publication metadata places the September 16 preprint inside the 30-day UTC window ending October 13; the experiment itself ran April 26–May 8, so the new development is its reported evidence, not a newly conducted run ([saved §4.3](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.3%20Research%20loop)). The authors report Git-linked experiments and negative results, with development performance improving from 3.3923 to 1.899044 bpb. Every component was selected on the same 200-text evaluator; the trained GPT-2 reference is not a matched coordination baseline, and the smallest gains fall below hardware variation ([saved §4.5](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.5%20Evidence)). Different-account verifications are internal checks, not independent external replication; one 'confirmed' discrepancy exceeded the stated approximate tolerance. The autonomy claim also needs qualification: humans changed prompts and search views together, and a manually launched session contributed to the winning ancestry ([saved §4.7](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.7%20Human%20intervention)). The authors did not rerun the winner and report missing evaluator logs and dependency/data pins ([saved §4.8](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.8%20How%20we%20verified)). Thirteen workers each had an 80-GB GPU, but the report supplies no complete monetary budget; student affordability and discovery efficiency are unestablished ([saved §4.2](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4.2%20Agents)). The builders evaluate their own system, an author-interest dependency rather than outside corroboration; no financial conflict is established by the supplied text ([saved experiment framing](data/assets/59b2cb8b434efeeb70a133bc/66025228eaffdbf60602a9c3e085782385578f7304cce9751aff2a52b9936729/text.txt#:~:text=4%20Experiments)). Editorial inference: useful for teaching provenance, negative-result retention and verification requirements, with protected test data and matched-budget comparisons needed before claiming general research gains.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480", "version_id": "7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept for concrete practitioner evidence about costly failures, memory and evaluation design. Supplied September 24 publication metadata falls within the 30-day UTC window ending October 13; novelty is the report of an earlier twelve-week campaign, whose exact calendar dates are not supplied. The paper explicitly frames its contribution as a failure taxonomy and cost-dependent use of standard mechanisms, not a new algorithm ([saved contributions](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=Contributions.)). Reported failures include eleven consecutive evaluator timeouts and repeated failed configurations; System A iterations took 9–19 hours on multiple GPUs, versus 6–52 minutes on one GPU for B. Costs are approximate rather than a complete campaign budget ([saved §§II-C–III](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=II-C%20Cost%20Profile)). Report the 1.82× Recall@6 gain as a peak offline result: the across-date mean supports 1.63×, and sequential component additions do not isolate causal effects ([saved §V-A](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=V-A%20System)). Examine, rather than repeat, the contradiction between §V-E's claim that an immutable evaluator prevents metric gaming and §III-E's documented coherence gaming through unusable singleton clusters ([saved validation claim](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=V-E%20Validation), [saved failure](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=III-E%20Metric%20Fixation)). Likewise, unsuccessful search does not prove the tradeoff mathematically unavoidable. System B used human strategic pivots and human-maintained instructions; these are not training the agent's weights ([saved §IV-D](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=IV-D%20Persistence)). Both systems belong to one Amazon book-recommendation setting, giving valuable practitioner experience but a shared organizational interest rather than external corroboration. The authors acknowledge observational ablations, unvalidated customer impact and limited generalization; proprietary purchase data prevent exact public replication, and no independent replication or outside researcher assessment is supplied ([saved limitations](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=Limitations.), [saved reproducibility statement](data/assets/7082835cef4c8540dcb8d480/7d04403761d8cb23614022d48ddb879a6de4fb7f5af821bb1d1d2cb773d97ec4/text.txt#:~:text=Reproducibility)). Editorial inference: students can test small loops, retain failure histories and budget human metric review without treating these reported gains as generally established.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "78deb02bb43b9240c74487b3", "version_id": "4c16684f04ac89de0cfd2e9942cde9c20a91e0d7aa7d934da6ede6eaa2463817", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied publication date, October 11, is within the run's preceding 30-day window as of October 13, 2026; the October 14 retrieval date does not establish novelty. This is a generic product/news roundup, not inspectable evidence about experimental automation. Its potentially relevant Epoch and ATLAS entries provide descriptions and outbound links, without the original studies' methods, budgets or results; those claims cannot be evaluated from this item. See the saved [AI resources passage](data/assets/78deb02bb43b9240c74487b3/4c16684f04ac89de0cfd2e9942cde9c20a91e0d7aa7d934da6ede6eaa2463817/text.txt#:~:text=AI%20resources). Reject the roundup rather than treating linked research as supplied supporting evidence or independent corroboration. The publisher promotes paid material in [“All my paid goodies in one place”](data/assets/78deb02bb43b9240c74487b3/4c16684f04ac89de0cfd2e9942cde9c20a91e0d7aa7d934da6ede6eaa2463817/text.txt#:~:text=All%20my%20paid%20goodies%20in%20one%20place); additional commercial relationships are not established by the supplied evidence.", "piece_ids": [], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "7f0901064878a294934bd154", "version_id": "6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied September 30 publication date falls within the run's 30-day window. Useful new evidence is the controlled comparison of minimal and elaborate research-agent harnesses, not the older benchmark literature. The authors report matched backbones, worker hardware and budgets, withheld MLE-bench test feedback, and component ablations ([Sections 3–4](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=3%20Experimental%20settings)). Their GLM comparison reports 62.5% self-selected medals for Malena versus 47.1% for AiScientist. However, the detailed tables qualify the broad 'matches or beats' language: Gemma significantly favors MLEvolve on percentile, and several other comparisons are inconclusive; absence of significance is not proof of equivalence ([D.2](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=D.2%20Detailed%20MLE-bench%20results)). Preserve the distinction between original default29 ablations and corrected fixed30 comparisons ([A.1–A.2](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=A.1%20MLE-bench%20tasks%20used)). NatureBench adds a second benchmark, not independent replication: unlimited evaluation queries and oracle selection create unequal scoring opportunities ([D.6](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=D.6%20NatureBench)). Costs are modeled, including an assumed cache discount; separate multi-GPU backbone serving from the single-A100 experiment worker ([A.4](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=A.4%20LLM%20backbones%20used)). This is an author-run preprint comparison: the authors acknowledge ownership of Malena, possible tuning asymmetry, contamination risk and only 3–4 seeds for 24-hour runs; independent replication and outside practitioner assessment are not supplied ([G.1](data/assets/7f0901064878a294934bd154/6c598d9a3db4f487a0045a147e48bc3e4064e2b81bf388f4ac0947b9d96c78ec/text.txt#:~:text=G.1%20Limitations)). Editorial inference: students should benchmark a simple agent first, protect evaluation data and measure selection quality and total cost. Accept for reporting and scrutiny, not as a universal demonstration that harnesses are useless.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "810ca788d6580a6871563f4d", "version_id": "2ec6998b1c53899734b6cb244fefc18311d1635c79e90220c4b2743ae1235252", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The supplied October 1 publication date is within the run's 30-day window, but the contribution is a tutoring prompt and flashcard workflow, not evidence about autonomous computational experiments. The author's puppy-training demonstration produces 37 cards without a controlled baseline, independently checked knowledge assessment or measured learning outcome ([demonstration](data/assets/810ca788d6580a6871563f4d/2ec6998b1c53899734b6cb244fefc18311d1635c79e90220c4b2743ae1235252/text.txt#:~:text=As%20a%20test)). Chatbot-generated diagnostic scores do not establish their accuracy. The recent workflow offers no qualifying experimental novelty for this series, despite its general student relevance. The author directly benefits from promoting a subscriber-only skill ([“Dig deeper”](data/assets/810ca788d6580a6871563f4d/2ec6998b1c53899734b6cb244fefc18311d1635c79e90220c4b2743ae1235252/text.txt#:~:text=Dig%20deeper)); its inaccessible paid implementation does not warrant deferral because the visible item's core subject is outside scope.", "piece_ids": [], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e", "version_id": "22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The supplied October 7 publication date is within the run's 30-day window. The new evidence is three segmentation search campaigns applying an existing protocol; the reference segmentation results are from 2024, not a new development. The authors describe an immutable evaluator, frozen architecture and split, keep/revert decisions, and 24 experiments per campaign with a one-hour training budget per trial—not one hour for the whole search ([Methods and experimental study](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=2%20Method)). This is directly useful for small, inspectable student experiments. Scrutiny must retain the conflicting modification outcomes: Dice helps the GX10 campaigns but hurts the 4070 baseline; model, hardware and configuration are confounded, so these observations do not isolate hardware causation ([3.1](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=3.1%20Retained%20modifications)). Only Loop B receives a test evaluation; trials use one seed, small retained gains lack variance estimates, and the historical GAN comparison is compute-unmatched. The displayed 0.836 versus 0.833 test IoUs differ by 0.003, whereas the prose says 0.002; flag this unresolved numerical inconsistency rather than infer an unreported precision correction ([3.2 and Table 3](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=3.2%20Comparison%20with%20the%20reference%20schedule)). A declared-space tuner comparison remains future work ([Conclusion](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=4%20Conclusion)). The [abstract's repository link](data/assets/a007976d7a6dcb8c99635a7e/22bcded05aecba83c6a4594604bdc843c3061c7ccdf19d4be43c9ea27beaec4f/text.txt#:~:text=Research%20repository) supports a reproducibility lead, not verified reproducibility. This is the investigators' preprint account, with no independent replication, outside practitioner assessment or commercial-conflict disclosure supplied. Editorial inference: freeze evaluation, budget the entire search, repeat promising trials and test transfer before adopting retained edits as defaults.", "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"], "retained_from": "runs/20261014T032814-a43e45/decisions.jsonl"}
+{"item_id": "ade5c65097bf35b3d1cb467e", "version_id": "5a82503b8b0e7e873cc96ddaa5b89b9957e647009d50cff4f549b940594dfeef", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept for a limited additional evidence-scrutiny role: a concrete cost claim students can learn to interrogate. September 29 publication metadata is within September 15–October 14, 2026 UTC; dates of the underlying work are unspecified. A founder describes an estimated annual analysis cost at maximum second-lab throughput of roughly $30 million and compression to below $1 million (s01100–s01116, [2613–2652.46s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/215855083/2affdef5ab1fade3557377735a882b58.mp3#t=2613,2652.46)). Treat this as a founder's account of projected economics, not audited savings or a general efficiency result: model identities, hardware, workload, accuracy parity, training expense, evaluation splits and replication are absent. The student implication is an editorial inference: compare total costs at matched quality and workload before adopting specialization. Preserve the throughput qualification: the introduction asserts thousands of experiments daily (s00023–s00024, 106.28–116.38s), while the detailed discussion frames that scale as a future objective (s00746–s00750, [1838.24–1849.86s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/215855083/2affdef5ab1fade3557377735a882b58.mp3#t=1838.24,1849.86)); current throughput is unestablished. The sample-holder correction anecdote (s00894–s00907, 2145.92–2176s) overlaps Latent Space s00232 and must not count as independent evidence. Commercial incentives are explicit in customer systems and retained-IP plans (s01206–s01223, [2848.96–2894.64s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/215855083/2affdef5ab1fade3557377735a882b58.mp3#t=2848.96,2894.64)). Accept the distinct cost-scrutiny example, not repeated marketing, PhD-equivalence claims or established speedups; independent researchers and inspectable supporting results remain missing.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
+{"item_id": "ead4cdfb34d1b428c1cd760b", "version_id": "2440cc1580de805fb537ea10d57c87f518177ce7fa5c4cf63e2260a65098b0dc", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept narrowly as a scientific-practitioner account contrasting physical and computational experiments. October 8 publication metadata falls within September 15–October 14, 2026 UTC; the recent contribution is the account's operational detail, not proof that its undated lab events happened within this window. Founders describe noisy telemetry (s00008, [169–288s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/219146438/4de3baad7036438bcc048cc532556c6a.mp3#t=169,288)), targeted automation with full autonomy explicitly a non-goal (s00230, [3046–3099s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/219146438/4de3baad7036438bcc048cc532556c6a.mp3#t=3046,3099)), and preserving scientific-process lineage (s00267, [3493–3524s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/219146438/4de3baad7036438bcc048cc532556c6a.mp3#t=3493,3524)). These support attributed examples and the editorial inference that students should automate measurable bottlenecks while retaining provenance. Preserve the correction: the host suggests an unambiguous observable, but the guests explicitly describe remaining phase ambiguity and replicates (s00072–s00078, [1377–1438s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/219146438/4de3baad7036438bcc048cc532556c6a.mp3#t=1377,1438)). No released datasets, controlled baselines, held-out results, ablations, quantified budgets or independent replication substantiate superior performance. Founders have a commercial interest, made explicit in customer deployment discussion (s00341, [4506–4613s](https://api.substack.com/feed/podcast/219146438/4de3baad7036438bcc048cc532556c6a.mp3#t=4506,4613)). Their Generalist appearance is the same interested source, not corroboration; independent researcher assessment remains missing.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
+{"item_id": "youtube-R9momwXV9w4", "version_id": "81ddd8b2230f42d36bc234d2235a06343303c4274511e44bb5cd8b1409bafab7", "decision": "defer", "reason": "September 24 publication metadata is within September 15–October 14, 2026 UTC, but the relevant new evaluation claims lack supplied original supporting documents. The commentator reports internal research-task scores and a replacement threshold (s00075–s00082, [426.72–471.92s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R9momwXV9w4&t=426)); no task inventory, baseline protocol, compute budget, hardware, held-out controls or reproducibility artifacts are supplied. The reported absence of sustained twofold acceleration (s00072–s00074, [408.72–426.72s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R9momwXV9w4&t=408)) and an external evaluator's purported probability of that acceleration (s00093–s00095, [527.6–542.88s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R9momwXV9w4&t=527)) require comparison of definitions, periods and uncertainty, not averaging or a declaration of contradiction. The 2024 commitments and July 2026 revisions discussed at s00085–s00099 are older events, not September developments. These issues could serve evidence scrutiny, but the video is secondary commentary dependent on unavailable-in-this-packet system cards and evaluations. Its creator also promotes their own benchmark (s00254, [1374.64–1379.52s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R9momwXV9w4&t=1374)); financial ties are unspecified. Lab claims have institutional interests, and excerpts of lab researchers do not supply independent replication. Defer pending original evidence; broader speculative forecasts add little to students' inspectable experiments.", "piece_ids": []}
+{"item_id": "youtube-wMQB33rM28I", "version_id": "91b5117a082251bc859d7cb81ba933c439e1b0450075c2bf98b2b8112bb7d58e", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Accept as an operational tutorial under revision 2, not evidence of measured improvement. Supplied publication metadata dates it October 11, within the inclusive September 15–October 14, 2026 UTC window. Its useful contribution is a small instruction-optimization procedure: the model remains unchanged (s00010–s00013, [51.34–69.6s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wMQB33rM28I&t=51)), grading is separated from editable instructions (s00053–s00058, [257.9–284.7s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wMQB33rM28I&t=257)), and final tasks are withheld from optimization (s00140–s00146, [645.86–674.34s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wMQB33rM28I&t=645)). The proposed budget totals 48 worker trials before optimizer and setup costs; this is planning arithmetic, not observed expenditure (s00160–s00170, [737.14–789.02s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wMQB33rM28I&t=737)). No inspectable execution logs, achieved baseline/held-out scores, ablations or independent replication accompany the supplied tutorial; hypothetical outcomes cannot establish gains (s00124–s00129 and s00147–s00157). Defer the contradictory automatic-transcript passage s00105 at 489.3–493.54s pending original-audio checking; do not attribute cherry-picking advice to the speaker. Adjacent s00103–s00104 separately support fixed repeat counts. Membership and donation appeals establish a channel monetization interest, not a demonstrated vendor sponsorship (s00000–s00003; s00194–s00195, [889.18–899.9s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wMQB33rM28I&t=889)). Useful for student evaluation design; no demonstrated new capability.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
